libstdcxx-nosized.patch - two sized operator delete calls of libstdc++ 13.3.0 become the unsized forms.

Why: the guest compiler runs with -fno-sized-deallocation (guest_compiler.json flags.semantics), under which the sized and
aligned-sized declarations of operator delete are not declared, so these two call sites do not compile
(src/c++17/fs_path.cc, the path list deallocation; src/c++17/memory_resource.cc, the new_delete_resource).
Equivalence: [new.delete.single] and [new.delete.array] define the default sized operator delete(void*, size_t) as
"calls operator delete(ptr)" (and the aligned-sized form as operator delete(ptr, align)), and the default operator
delete[](void*, size_t) likewise forwards to operator delete[](ptr). The size argument carries no other effect in the default
functions, so the unsized call has the same behaviour for the default operators; a user replacement of the unsized form is
what both calls reach. In memory_resource.cc the aligned case calls the aligned unsized form ([new.delete.single], align_val_t).
check_mirror.py C6 proves no sized symbol is referenced in the pack.

--- gcc-13.3.0/libstdc++-v3/src/c++17/fs_path.cc
+++ gcc-13.3.0/libstdc++-v3/src/c++17/fs_path.cc
@@ -267,7 +267,7 @@
     {
       __glibcxx_assert(p->_M_size <= p->_M_capacity);
       p->clear();
-      ::operator delete(p, sizeof(*p) + p->_M_capacity * sizeof(value_type));
+      ::operator delete(p);
     }
 }
 
--- gcc-13.3.0/libstdc++-v3/src/c++17/memory_resource.cc
+++ gcc-13.3.0/libstdc++-v3/src/c++17/memory_resource.cc
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
       void
       do_deallocate(void* __p, size_t __bytes, size_t __alignment) noexcept
       override
-      { ::operator delete(__p, __bytes, std::align_val_t(__alignment)); }
+      { ::operator delete(__p, std::align_val_t(__alignment)); }
 
       bool
       do_is_equal(const memory_resource& __other) const noexcept override
